      "sha256": "267af54481f344e806d4cb3ad602aa7f32020b930845e2aa152b7daaa2f9a440",
      "lines": [
        223,
        234
      ],
      "text": "Global squarefreeness remains in the physical coefficient and its density.\nIt is removed only in the analytic tensor expansion.  If the support is\n$D_*\\le N^{\\theta_*}$ with $\\theta_*<1$, the change in the discrepancy\nis at most a fixed divisor factor times\n\\begin{align}\n &\\sum_{\\substack{q\\le D_*\\\\p^2\\mid q\\text{ for some }p\\ge N^{\\eta_0}}}\n \\left(\\frac{N}{q}+1+\\frac{N}{\\varphi(q)}\\right)\n \\ll (N+D_*)N^{-\\eta_0+o(1)}.\n \\label{coef:collision}\n\\end{align}\nThe term $1$ includes an exact complete product equal to $N$.\nNo divisor function is evaluated at zero.",
      "scope": "Squarefree collision and exact complete product equality are separate costs."
    },
